## Likely follow-up questions

**Q: Depth in nodes or edges?**

Ask. LeetCode counts nodes; some interviewers count edges (one less).

**Q: Empty tree?**

0.

**Q: Complexity?**

O(n) time; O(width) memory for BFS, O(h) for DFS.

**Q: Recursive version?**

Three lines: 1 + max(left, right). Say it overflows on a deep chain, and offer BFS.

**Q: Shared state?**

Read-only tree.

**Q: Minimum depth on a huge tree.**

BFS wins: it stops at the first leaf; DFS must visit everything.

**Q: How would you test it?**

Empty, single node, lopsided, a deep chain, and a shallow leaf next to a deep branch.

